## 1. Initial Enterprise Assessment

An enterprise-wide assessment was performed to evaluate Secure Boot certificate readiness across approximately **3,800 Windows devices**.

The assessment identified the following certificate states:

| Certificate Status                    | Device Count |
| ------------------------------------- | -----------: |
| CERTS ACTIVE + Secure Boot Enabled    |          683 |
| CERTS ACTIVE + Secure Boot Disabled   |           15 |
| CERTS INACTIVE + Secure Boot Enabled  |          998 |
| CERTS INACTIVE + Secure Boot Disabled |           38 |
| CERTS MISSING + Secure Boot Enabled   |         1549 |
| CERTS MISSING + Secure Boot Disabled  |          120 |
| CERTS MISSING + Secure Boot Unknown   |            7 |

This assessment was used to determine the appropriate remediation strategy based on Microsoft's Secure Boot Certificate Expiration (2026) guidance.
